# Trivy CVE suppression — reviewed and accepted risks
#
# CVE-2026-24049  wheel <=0.45.1  (Privilege Escalation via malicious wheel file)
# CVE-2026-23949  jaraco.context <=5.3.0  (Path traversal via malicious tar archive)
#
# Both vulnerabilities are triggered only during package installation, not at runtime.
# The standalone packages are already upgraded (wheel 0.47.0, jaraco.context 6.1.2).
# The remaining findings come from setuptools' private _vendor/ directory, which is
# an internal build-toolchain copy never invoked by the running FastAPI container.
# Suppressing here is the correct response; upgrading setuptools does not resolve
# the vendored paths in the version shipped with python:3.11-slim-bookworm.
CVE-2026-24049
CVE-2026-23949
